--- INC41220398#symptom (1129 chars)
Incident INC41220398: System will not allow member check-in due to insurance profile problems
Affected service: Member Profile
Description: A prior ticket was submitted for this problem and mistakenly marked resolved. On check-in for a single member, a pop-up states the member has not successfully retrieved a profile from the enrollment system. This is occurring for only one member; local enrollment staff confirm all fields are populated correctly on their end and believe it is a platform-level defect.
Initial notes: On check-in a pop-up appears: 'The current member has not successfully retrieved a profile from the enrollment system.' This member has been seen before and enrollment co-workers report everything is correct on their end. | Transferring to Member Profile. The correlation identifier does not exist and the integration engine treats this as an error, producing a correlation-not-found error rather than sending partial demographic data. Proposed action: Member Profile sends the correlation add to the identity registry. Broader effort: reconciliation of the correlation-to-registry-ID gap remains in scope.

--- INC41220398#resolution (371 chars)
Incident INC41220398: System will not allow member check-in due to insurance profile problems
Resolution code: Solved (Permanently)
Technical cause: Errors/Drops
Caused by change: No
Resolution notes: Correlation sent to the identity registry to resolve the correlation issue.
Final work note: Correlation add sent to the identity registry to resolve the correlation gap.

